Bug: browsing from inside a macro body needs a batch -create

The server alone answers "No reference" where the same navigation works once
-create has run. findMacroExpansionFile (src/cxref.c) picks a CU by looking for
a UsageMacroBaseFileUsage reference; expandMacroCall adds one only in XrefMode
(src/yylex.c:2530), so in a server-only session no CU is ever found.

Removing the XrefMode condition is not enough: the reference is then created
(verified 2026-09-18) but the answer stays "No reference", so something else on
that path is missing too. Start by finding what consumes the reference after
the expansion file is parsed.

expected is the answer test_browsing_push_in_unexpanded_macro gets with -create;
only the first two lines differ, since this test runs no create step.
